# Ether Themes — Core

Token-driven **VS Code / Cursor extension**: **8 dark palettes** → generated color themes, 392 snippets → generated `.code-snippets`. No runtime extension code — everything is build-time generation.

Palette authoring uses an **anchor-first** workflow (`surfacePanel` + `surfaceEditor` first, then surfaces → foreground → accent → syntax). See `ether-themes.mdc` for the full convention and current theme table.

## Architecture

```
src/palettes/*.js          → src/generator/ + src/workbench/ + src/syntax/
                           → themes/*.color-theme.json

src/snippets/catalog/*.js  → src/snippets/generator.js + validate.js
                           → snippets/*.code-snippets

src/build.js               → runs both pipelines, syncs package.json contributes
```

## Source of truth vs generated

| Edit these | Never hand-edit |
|------------|-----------------|
| `src/palettes/`, `src/workbench/`, `src/syntax/`, `src/utils/` | `themes/*.color-theme.json` |
| `src/snippets/catalog/` (non-synced modules) | `snippets/*.code-snippets` |
| `src/generator/`, `src/snippets/generator.js`, tests | `package.json` → `contributes.themes` / `contributes.snippets` |

After any source change, run `npm run build`. Use `npm run check` (lint + test + build) before claiming work is complete.

## Code style

- **ESM only** (`import`/`export`), Node 20+, plain JavaScript with JSDoc types (no TypeScript).
- Match existing naming: `ether-{name}` palette ids (8 dark themes: graphite, storm, ember, luna, moss, dusk, ink, stone), kebab-case snippet keys, 4-space indent in palettes.
- **Minimal diffs** — reuse `src/utils/color.js` helpers and existing derivation patterns; don't duplicate logic.
- **JSDoc** on exported functions/types: `@param`, `@returns`, `@throws` when relevant; skip trivial one-liners and data-only exports.
- **Tests**: Vitest in `tests/` — add coverage for new validation rules, derivation keys, or catalog invariants.

## Agent constraints

- Do not commit, push, publish, or bump version unless explicitly asked.
- Do not skip CI hooks or force-push.
- README/CHANGELOG updates only when the user requests docs changes.
- Preview themes via **F5** (Extension Development Host), not by editing generated JSON.
